challenges.description:
What does `A & B` mean, and what must a value satisfy to be assignable to it?

  type Timestamped = { createdAt: string }
  type Named = { name: string }
  type TimestampedNamed = Timestamped & Named

  const x: TimestampedNamed = ???

Given:

  type A = { x: number }
  type B = { y: string }

  type Union = A | B         // what can you safely access?
  type Intersection = A & B  // what can you safely access?

What do the overload signatures define, and what is the implementation signature's role?

  function parse(input: string): number
  function parse(input: number): string
  function parse(input: string | number): string | number {
    return typeof input === 'string' ? parseInt(input, 10) : String(input)
  }
